{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3368","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3368","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3368\",\"parent_revision\":\"1e58192c4304c45fd511a1e83bbb8e2a7598b45d5fc76a8ff0696116c4fee4eb\",\"root_revision\":\"1e58192c4304c45fd511a1e83bbb8e2a7598b45d5fc76a8ff0696116c4fee4eb\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-01\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nPR #3367 gave 42 of `backlog_core/server.py`'s 43 `@mcp.tool` functions a real Pydantic return type, so FastMCP's `outputSchema` advertises actual field names instead of the unconstrained `{\\\"additionalProperties\\\": true, \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\"}` every tool had before. `backlog_view` is the one tool deliberately left untyped \u2014 it's tracked by name in `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_tool_output_schemas.py`'s `TOOLS_NOT_YET_TYPED` set, with a comment explaining why, but nothing outside the codebase pointed at this until now.\\n\\nWhy it was deferred: `backlog_view` returns one of 7 structurally different shapes depending on the call \u2014 map mode, navigate mode, extract mode, a compact summary, an over-budget view, a full-detail view, and several distinct error shapes (ordinal-not-found, param error, section-filter-miss, generic BacklogError). Every other tool in the rollout collapses to one flat model; this one is closer to seven tools' worth of design work in a single function, which is disproportionate to the rest of the batch.\\n\\nWhat's already known, so whoever picks this up doesn't have to re-derive it:\\n- FastMCP forbids a `Union` as a tool's *return type annotation* \u2014 verified against `fastmcp/tools/function_parsing.py`'s `_is_object_schema`, which doesn't recognize `anyOf`, so a `ModelA | ModelB` return type gets silently wrapped (`x-fastmcp-wrap-result: True`), nesting `structured_content` under `{\\\"result\\\": ...}` \u2014 a wire-protocol regression.\\n- A `Union` used *as a field* inside one wrapper model is fine \u2014 only a union at the annotation root trips the wrap bug. So the shape to build is one flat `BacklogViewResponse(BaseModel)` with something like `response: MapView | NavigateView | ExtractView | SummaryView | OverBudgetView | FullDetailView | SectionMissError | GenericError`.\\n- The full-detail branch already has real infrastructure to reuse: `ViewItemResult` (`backlog_core/models.py`) is a complete existing model, including its `sections: dict[str, SectionEntryMetadata | GroomedSectionMetadata]` field \u2014 the dynamic section-name keys are not an obstacle, pydantic validates that fine.\\n- Token budget: after the 42-tool rollout, the schema-test's total budget (`plugins/development-harness/tests/test_tool_output_schemas.py`) sits around 9900 of a 13000-token ceiling \u2014 roughly 3000 tokens of headroom for this one tool, which should be enough but is worth measuring rather than assuming (the test file has a `_schema_tokens` helper already wired for exactly this).\\n- Established patterns to follow: every tool returns `SomeResponse.model_validate({...}).model_dump(exclude_none=True)` (a plain dict, not the raw model instance) so runtime wire shape is unchanged; every `X | None` field needs an explicit `= None` default or FastMCP's output validation fails at call time the moment the real value is `None` (a real bug hit twice during the rollout \u2014 `Milestone.due_on` and `IssueEntry.milestone`).\\n\\nAcceptance criteria:\\n- [ ] `backlog_view`'s return type is a real Pydantic model (or a wrapper with a field-level discriminated union), not `dict[str, object]`.\\n- [ ] Remove `backlog_view` from `TOOLS_NOT_YET_TYPED` in `tests/test_tool_output_schemas.py` once typed; the existing schema/budget assertions must pass for it like every other tool.\\n- [ ] Full `plugins/development-harness` test suite (`tests/`, `tests_backlog/`, `backlog_core/tests/`, `tests_sam/`, `sam_schema/tests/`) still green.\\n- [ ] `ruff check` / `ty check` clean.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Follow-up from PR #3367 (FastMCP typed-output rollout)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-01\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"11351c33b4662c0321c8c9daf607698d74c5466de2d5aa27b5abd686505f7739\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABR0jMRw\"}"}